{"id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#prop:density-transformation-law","title":"prop:density-transformation-law","path":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2.md","line":2009,"body":"","kind":"theorem","status":"not_started","tex":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2.tex#prop:density-transformation-law","uses":["[[references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#prop:density-abs-det]]","[[references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:density-vector-space]]"],"inspired_by":[],"bindings":[],"is_index":false,"body_html":"","formal":[],"tex_content":{"path":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2.tex","label":"prop:density-transformation-law","line":3219,"source":"\\begin{proposition}[The Transformation Law]\n\\label{prop:density-transformation-law}\n\n\\uses{prop:density-abs-det, def:density-vector-space}\n\n\n\n\nFor linear $f:V\\to V$,\n\\[\n|fv_1\\wedge\\cdots\\wedge fv_n|=|\\det f|\\,|v_1\\wedge\\cdots\\wedge v_n|.\n\\]\nThus the inner-product density satisfies Definition \\ref{def:density-vector-space}.\n\\end{proposition}\n\n\\begin{proof}\n\n\\uses{prop:density-abs-det}\n\\sketch In an orthonormal basis, the coefficient matrix of $(fv_j)$ is $AM$, where $A$ represents $f$ and $M$ represents $(v_j)$. Proposition \\ref{prop:density-abs-det} gives $|\\det(AM)|=|\\det f|\\,|\\det M|$.\n\\end{proof}","html":" <p></p><section class=\"theorem\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Proposition</div></section>[The Transformation Law] <span class=\"tex-label\" id=\"tex-label-70726f703a64656e736974792d7472616e73666f726d6174696f6e2d6c6177\"></span> <p></p><a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23prop%3Adensity-abs-det\">↗ prop:density-abs-det</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23def%3Adensity-vector-space\">↗ def:density-vector-space</a> <p></p>For linear <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$f:V\\to V$\">$f:V\\to V$</span>, <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"true\" data-tex=\"\\[  |fv_1\\wedge \\cdots \\wedge fv_n|=|\\det f|\\, |v_1\\wedge \\cdots \\wedge v_n|.  \\]\">\\[  |fv_1\\wedge \\cdots \\wedge fv_n|=|\\det f|\\, |v_1\\wedge \\cdots \\wedge v_n|.  \\]</span> Thus the inner-product density satisfies Definition <a class=\"reference tex-ref\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23def%3Adensity-vector-space\" data-tex-node=\"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:density-vector-space\" data-tex-anchor=\"tex-label-6465663a64656e736974792d766563746f722d7370616365\">12.1</a>.  <p></p><section class=\"theorem proof\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Proof</div><p><a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23prop%3Adensity-abs-det\">↗ prop:density-abs-det</a> \\sketch In an orthonormal basis, the coefficient matrix of <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$(fv_j)$\">$(fv_j)$</span> is <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$AM$\">$AM$</span>, where <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$A$\">$A$</span> represents <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$f$\">$f$</span> and <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$M$\">$M$</span> represents <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$(v_j)$\">$(v_j)$</span>. Proposition <a class=\"reference tex-ref\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23prop%3Adensity-abs-det\" data-tex-node=\"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#prop:density-abs-det\" data-tex-anchor=\"tex-label-70726f703a64656e736974792d6162732d646574\">9</a> gives <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$|\\det (AM)|=|\\det f|\\, |\\det M|$\">$|\\det (AM)|=|\\det f|\\, |\\det M|$</span>. </p><span class=\"qed\" aria-label=\"证毕\" style=\"display:block;text-align:right\">□</span></section>","warnings":["部分 TeX 排版细节未完整还原（已保留可读内容）: sketch"]},"previous":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#prop:density-value-one","next":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#prop:density-positive","relations":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#prop:density-abs-det","title":"prop:density-abs-det","label":"prop:density-abs-det"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:density-vector-space","title":"def:density-vector-space","label":"def:density-vector-space"}],"backlinks":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#prop:density-uniqueness-pointwise","title":"prop:density-uniqueness-pointwise","label":"prop:density-uniqueness-pointwise"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#prop:riemannian-density","title":"prop:riemannian-density","label":"prop:riemannian-density"}],"copy_context":{"version":1,"level":0,"node":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#prop:density-transformation-law","title":"prop:density-transformation-law","tex":"\\begin{proposition}[The Transformation Law]\n\\label{prop:density-transformation-law}\n\n\\uses{prop:density-abs-det, def:density-vector-space}\n\n\n\n\nFor linear $f:V\\to V$,\n\\[\n|fv_1\\wedge\\cdots\\wedge fv_n|=|\\det f|\\,|v_1\\wedge\\cdots\\wedge v_n|.\n\\]\nThus the inner-product density satisfies Definition \\ref{def:density-vector-space}.\n\\end{proposition}\n\n\\begin{proof}\n\n\\uses{prop:density-abs-det}\n\\sketch In an orthonormal basis, the coefficient matrix of $(fv_j)$ is $AM$, where $A$ represents $f$ and $M$ represents $(v_j)$. Proposition \\ref{prop:density-abs-det} gives $|\\det(AM)|=|\\det f|\\,|\\det M|$.\n\\end{proof}","source":"tex/references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2.tex",